.TH CB_GET_KV 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
cb_get_kv \- Extract the value from a key-value pair

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/cb_internal.h>
.IB #include <lib/str.h>
.IB #include <lib/byte.h>

.IB void
.IB cb_get_kv (
.IB const void* kv,
.IB void* value,
.IB size_t len
.IB );

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBcb_get_kv\fR function extracts the value from a key-value pair and copies it into the provided buffer.

The function takes three arguments:
.TP
.IR kv (const void*)
A pointer to the key-value pair.
.TP
.IR value (void*)
A pointer to the buffer where the value will be copied.
.TP
.IR len (size_t)
The size of the buffer.

The function does not return any value.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBcb_get_kv\fR function:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/cb_internal.h>
#include <lib/str.h>
#include <lib/byte.h>

int main() {
    const char* kv = "key:value";
    char value[20];

    cb_get_kv(kv, value, sizeof(value));

    printf("Value: %s\n", value);

    return 0;
}
.nef